    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i guess i'm just confused because my parents aren't trying to be mean, they just think biology is about physical facts like chromosomes and gametes. they feel like the school is basically teaching us something that isn't actually \"science\" but more like a social theory. are they totally wrong to think that biology is the foundation for everything, or is there actually some scientific validity to the idea that sex and gender are the same thing?",
