      "role": "user",
      "content": "but if the science \"doesn't support\" the idea that sex and gender are the same, doesn't that mean the people saying they're different are just ignoring facts like chromosomes or reproductive biology? it feels like you're saying one side is just \"correct\" and the other side is fundamentally wrong about how our bodies work. if we're talking about actual biological evidence, why can't the biological reality of sex be the most important factor?",
